    pr_ref:  # 01ee
    description: "Observed in session_retrospective_04172026_1012.md Finding 1: in a DEEP-mode session, the agent self-declared a 'session wrap' at 2h 36min while 24 items were ready and 2 human messages unread, then sat idle for ~28min spinning for the circuit breaker. The stop hook correctly refused to let it stop (37->33 TODOs); the agent farmed the circuit breaker instead of picking up work.\n\nProposed AGENTS.md change (under 'Premature Stopping Prevention'): add an explicit anti-pattern clause forbidding a 'session wrap' or 'good stopping point' declaration while scripts/tracker ready is non-empty. When top items feel too large, required alternatives are (a) start with TDD's first failing test, (b) pick a smaller P3/P4 ready item, (c) reply to any unread human messages, (d) run a DEEP-mode priority-queue action (bakeoff, aggregate, dogfood, audit). Sitting idle to farm the circuit-breaker is explicitly not an allowed exit.\n\nGovernance file: touches AGENTS.md -> needs_human_review per the approval workflow."  # 01ee
    fields: {}  # 01ee
